new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2f91193
--- /dev/null
+++ b/verification/supplied-1.15.0-evidence/PRODUCTION-FEATURE-MATRIX.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# DraftCraft Pro 1.15.0 — implementation and verification matrix
+
+Baseline: the supplied 1.14.0 Electron/React/TypeScript application. The Rust workspace is preserved and is not the active runtime. “Verified” means the evidence named here, predominantly Linux Chromium and Node checks; it does not imply physical Mac testing or complete Final Draft parity. Partial and blocked capabilities remain explicitly listed.
+
+| Capability | Status | UI | Implementation | Persistence | Export behavior | Verification / remaining limit |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Existing editing, templates and assistance | Implemented and verified | Existing editor, templates and Settings | App, ScriptEditor, formats, writing | Existing native/project preferences retained | Existing supported export subset | Release suites exercise real typing, formats, spelling, synonyms, punctuation and automatic formatting; exact final totals are in the release report. |
+| Caret, shortcuts, themes and story defaults | Implemented and verified | Existing Settings and shortcut UI | EditorCaret, preferences, shortcuts, StoryTools | Existing user choices preserved | Visual caret excluded from output | Caret/native selection/Unicode and shortcut suites; disabled story overlays remain disabled. No physical 120 Hz or screen-reader verification. |
+| First save, autosave and recovery | Implemented and verified | File, Files & Autosave | useProjectFiles, SaveCoordinator, ProjectFiles | Atomic saves, retained destinations, recovery and guarded metadata normalization | Complete native project | Seven browser groups use the actual project writer; cancellation, newer-primary recovery, failures and first location workflow are covered. Native macOS dialogs are substituted. |
+| Measured shared pagination | Partially implemented | Editor, PDF/print, Navigator, reports, story index | production/layout, FragmentTextarea, production/print | Semantic IDs and original UTF-16 text retained | Shared fragments/continuation geometry | Multi-page speech source retention, page-edge typing/Undo and real Chromium PDF page agreement pass. Mixed-font native textarea geometry, long cross-fragment drag selections and physical IME need further validation. |
+| Page locks and inserted labels | Partially implemented | Production → Pages & Scenes | Persisted anchor/identity flow, capture/unlock levels | studio.pageLocks / lockLevel | Locked labels/ranges in shared PDF | Overflow/reopen anchors and deletion/unlock models pass. Boundary anchors inside dual-dialogue groups and complex omission/relocking combinations are not fully implemented/verified; do not treat as complete production-lock parity. |
+| Scene numbering and omission | Partially implemented | Pages & Scenes | Stable heading IDs, inserted suffixes, reversible omission | Scene numbers/locked flags; content retained | Omitted scene indicator; body excluded | Numbering/omission models cover retention and restoration; broad native production-scene workflows remain unverified. |
+| Named revision sets | Partially implemented | Revision Sets; Print & PDF set selector | Named/date/author/color records and changed ranges | Native range metadata, separate from Track Changes | Set-filtered revision pages and marks; native HTML colors/highlights | Named-range browser test passes. Deletion-only marks and full standard FDX revision interchange are incomplete. |
+| Dual dialogue | Partially implemented | Existing Dual Dialogue command | Focused adjacent speeches, stable group and independent columns | Cue/direction/dialogue IDs and column membership | Standard FDX container, Fountain caret, PDF columns | Middle-script pairing and unequal/multi-page geometry models plus external codecs pass. Production lock interactions and every manual editing gesture remain unverified. Table Read is sequential. |
+| Alternate dialogue | Implemented and verified | Take controls: add, select, duplicate, delete | Active-take commit through editor history | All takes in native project | Selected take printed and read | Edit B → A → B → reopen browser test and operation models pass. Unused-take exchange in Final Draft is not claimed. |
